### api/me -- every request the module serves
#
# Needs an Auth0 access token for the Gradfolio API audience. Locally: log in
# through the frontend and open http://localhost:3000/auth/access-token
# (docs/auth0-setup.md §7); put the token in .env as `accessToken=…`.

@baseUrl = {{$dotenv baseUrl}}
@accessToken = {{$dotenv accessToken}}

###
# @name me
# 200 the caller's account. The first call after a login creates it from the
# token's claims (name, email, picture); later calls return the same id.
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###
# @name meWithoutToken
# 401 {"code":"UNAUTHENTICATED","message":"authentication required"},
# with WWW-Authenticate: Bearer. Nothing is created.
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/me

###
# @name meWithBadToken
# 401, the same body: the response never says why a token failed.
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer not.a.token

###
# @name completeOnboarding
# 200 {"onboarded":true}. Idempotent; GET /v1/me then shows onboarded: true.
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/me/onboarding/complete
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###
# @name deleteMe
# 204. Irreversible: the profile, sections, skills, projects, integrations and
# notifications are gone; your name stays on other people's projects without a
# photo. Sign out afterwards: a token that is still valid creates a new, empty
# account on the next request.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
